---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — Liv"
  description="Terms of use for Liv."
  ogUrl="https://hello.liv4all.com/terms"
>
  <div class="container">
    <a href="/" class="back">← back to liv4all</a>

    <h1>terms of use</h1>
    <p class="updated">last updated: 11 april 2026</p>

    <div class="callout">
      these terms are written in plain language on purpose. if something is unclear, reach out — we'd rather explain than hide behind legalese.
    </div>

    <h2>what this is</h2>
    <p>
      liv is an <strong>AI chief of staff in active development</strong>, operated by <strong>Liv4All</strong> (<strong>ABN 52 893 209 032</strong>), a registered business name of Leonardo Borges Barbosa, based in Zetland, NSW 2017, Australia, reachable at <a href="mailto:support@agent.liv4all.com">support@agent.liv4all.com</a>. "Liv4All", "we", "us", and "our" in these terms refer to that entity. by creating an account or otherwise using liv, you acknowledge and agree to the terms below.
    </p>
    <p>
      these terms govern your use of the liv4all product dashboard at <a href="https://app.liv4all.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://app.liv4all.com/</a> and this marketing site at <a href="https://hello.liv4all.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://hello.liv4all.com/</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>the basics</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>access is invite-only</strong> and can be revoked at any time, for any reason, with or without notice.</li>
      <li><strong>the service is provided as-is</strong>, with no guarantees of uptime, accuracy, or availability.</li>
      <li><strong>we may change, pause, or shut down the service</strong> at any point. we'll give active users reasonable notice wherever practical.</li>
      <li><strong>your feedback is welcome</strong> — it's how we make this better.</li>
      <li><strong>minimum age: 18.</strong> liv is not for minors.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>fair use</h2>
    <p>
      liv is designed to be a personal productivity assistant. we ask that you use it reasonably:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>don't abuse the service with excessive automated requests or load testing.</li>
      <li>don't attempt to reverse-engineer, extract, or resell the underlying models or infrastructure.</li>
      <li>don't use liv to spam, harass, or impersonate others.</li>
      <li>one account per person. don't share your access or bot credentials.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>ethical & legal use</h2>
    <p>
      this is the important one. you agree to use liv <strong>only for lawful and ethical purposes</strong>. specifically, you must not use liv to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>break the law</strong> — don't use liv to facilitate, plan, or carry out any illegal activity in your jurisdiction.</li>
      <li><strong>harm others</strong> — no harassment, threats, hate speech, stalking, doxxing, or any form of abuse directed at others.</li>
      <li><strong>generate harmful content</strong> — don't attempt to produce content that is violent, exploitative, deceptive, or designed to mislead.</li>
      <li><strong>compromise security</strong> — don't use liv to attack systems, phish, distribute malware, or gain unauthorised access to anything.</li>
      <li><strong>violate privacy</strong> — don't use liv to collect, store, or process other people's personal data without their consent.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>in short:</strong> use liv the way you'd want others to use powerful tools — responsibly, ethically, and without causing harm. if you're unsure whether something is okay, it probably isn't.
    </div>

    <h2>your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>liv stores conversation history and preferences to provide a persistent assistant experience.</li>
      <li>your data is <strong>not sold, not shared beyond the subprocessors listed in our privacy policy, and never used to train generalised AI/ML models</strong> — including data received from Google APIs and messages forwarded to your agent's inbox.</li>
      <li>you can request deletion of your data at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:support@agent.liv4all.com">support@agent.liv4all.com</a>. full deletion is completed within 30 days.</li>
      <li>for the complete picture — what we collect, how it's processed, where it lives, subprocessors, security controls, and your rights — see our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>connecting Google Workspace</h2>
    <p>
      liv connects to Google Workspace on your behalf. every scope is shown to you on Google's consent screen before access is granted. the scopes liv requests are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Calendar</strong> — to check availability, create and update events, and manage invites.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Contacts (read-only)</strong> — to find the right person when you ask liv to schedule or reach out to someone.</li>
      <li><strong>Gmail — modify</strong> (<code>gmail.modify</code>) — the single Gmail permission liv requests. it lets liv read and summarise your inbox, draft replies in your drafts folder, send drafted messages <em>only after you explicitly confirm</em>, create and manage labels, archive handled threads, and mark messages as read during inbox triage.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>liv will never permanently delete email from your account.</strong> the <code>gmail.modify</code> scope explicitly does not grant permanent-delete capability. any message liv moves is recoverable by you from your Gmail Trash or All Mail folder.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>liv will never use your Gmail data for advertising, credit scoring, lending decisions, or any financial-eligibility determination.</strong> these are hard red lines described in more detail in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>every scope above is optional.</strong> Google's consent screen lets you uncheck any scope you don't want to grant before approving the connection. liv is designed to work with whatever subset you grant — features that depend on a scope you declined will simply be unavailable. you can add or remove scopes later by re-running the connection, and revoke everything at once from your Google account permissions page.
    </p>
    <p>
      your use of Google Workspace through liv is also governed by <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Terms of Service</a>. you can revoke liv's access at any time via <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google account permissions</a>; liv will stop accessing Gmail, Calendar, and Contacts immediately, and any cached Gmail content is purged within 24 hours.
    </p>
    <p>
      liv4all's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs to any other app will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>AI agent responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      AI agents provided through our services are <strong>not legal persons</strong> and have no independent legal standing, rights, or authority. you acknowledge and agree that:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>you are solely responsible</strong> for all actions, omissions, and outputs of any AI agent operating on your behalf — including any communications sent, transactions made, or data accessed by your agent.</li>
      <li><strong>you should review agent actions</strong> where possible, particularly for communications sent to third parties, financial transactions, and calendar changes.</li>
      <li><strong>your agent acts on your instructions.</strong> any action your agent takes is treated as if you took that action yourself.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>the draft-first principle.</strong> liv <strong>always drafts before it sends</strong>. any outbound email liv composes on your behalf is first created as a real draft in your Gmail drafts folder (via <code>gmail.modify</code>) and surfaced to you for review. liv will only call the send API after you explicitly confirm the specific draft. the same principle applies to calendar invites sent to third-party attendees, and to any message liv sends through a connected messaging channel. this safeguard is enforced at the backend, not just in prompting, and cannot be disabled by the agent on its own.
    </div>

    <h2>liability</h2>
    <p>
      liv is an AI. it can make mistakes — miss a detail, misunderstand a request, or get something wrong. <strong>liv4all does not guarantee the accuracy, completeness, or appropriateness of any action taken by an AI agent.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      to the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any errors, losses, damages, or consequences arising from your use of the service or any actions taken by your AI agent — including but not limited to incorrect communications, missed appointments, erroneous bookings, or unintended data access.
    </p>

    <h2>changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      we may update these terms as the product evolves. we'll notify active users of any material changes. continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.
    </p>

    <h2>contact</h2>
    <p>
      questions? reach out at <a href="mailto:support@agent.liv4all.com">support@agent.liv4all.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .back {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }

  h1 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .updated {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 40px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  p, li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  p strong, li strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  li { margin-bottom: 8px; }

  .callout {
    background: var(--surface-glass);
    backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-light);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 20px 24px;
    margin: 32px 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .callout strong { color: var(--text); }

  code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.82em;
    color: var(--text);
    background: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.1);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-light);
  }
</style>
